  "layout_note": "Single-page front-matter legend in the NT (1582 Rhemes), between the Preface (idx 23) and 'THE BOOKES OF THE NEVV Teſtament' (idx 25). No running header and no printed folio; the display heading IS the section title. Centred graduated-roman display heading (3 lines: large caps 'THE SIGNIFICATION OR MEANING', smaller caps 'OF THE NVMBERS AND MARKES', roman lowercase 'vſed in this Nevv Teſtament.'). Below, a single wide measure of legend entries in a SMALL roman fount; a 2-line ornamental drop-cap 'T' opens entry 1. Entries 5-9 and 12 are prefixed by a mark-glyph set in the left mark-column (†, a raised double-comma mark, *, a faint 'other-reading' mark, a four-dot mark + ref-letters c b, and a leftward-barbed end-mark); entries 10-11 are the abbreviations 'Mt.'/'Mr.'. Gathering signature 'd' at foot-centre; catchword 'THE' at foot-right (next page opens 'THE BOOKES OF THE NEVV Teſtament', so catchword excluded from body). Heavy facing-page bleed-through/offset across the whole leaf (reversed ghost text + a dark offset 'V' at the far left of line 0). ONE glyph regime on this page: the small legend fount sets 'w' as GAPPED 'vv' throughout (matches the Preface's small dense-measure/marginal-note fount, NOT its large connected-w drop-cap fount).",
  "body": [
    {"line_index": 0, "role": "title_display", "text": "THE SIGNIFICATION OR MEANING", "note": "large graduated display caps; a dark offset/bleed 'V' sits at the far left before 'THE' (facing-page set-off, NOT part of the heading)"},
    {"line_index": 1, "role": "title_display", "text": "OF THE NVMBERS AND MARKES", "note": "smaller display caps; NVMBERS = u/v swap"},
    {"line_index": 2, "role": "subtitle", "text": "vſed in this Nevv Teſtament.", "note": "roman lowercase; vſed = u/v + long-ſ; Nevv = gapped vv"},
    {"line_index": 3, "role": "list_item", "text": "THE numbers in the inner margent of the text, ſhevv the num-", "drop_cap": "T", "line_end_hyphen": true, "note": "2-line ornamental drop-cap 'T'; 'ſhevv' = long-ſ + gapped vv; 'margent' as printed"},
    {"line_index": 4, "role": "list_item", "text": "ber of verſes in euery Chapter."},
    {"line_index": 5, "role": "list_item", "text": "The numbers in the Arguments before euery Chapter, point to"},
    {"line_index": 6, "role": "list_item", "text": "the ſame numbers of verſes in the text, treating of the ſame"},
    {"line_index": 7, "role": "list_item", "text": "matter."},
    {"line_index": 8, "role": "list_item", "text": "The numbers in the beginning of the Annotations, ſignifie, that"},
    {"line_index": 9, "role": "list_item", "text": "the Annotation is vpon ſuch a verſe of the text."},
    {"line_index": 10, "role": "list_item", "text": "The numbers in the inner margent, or els vvhere, ioyned to the ci-", "line_end_hyphen": true, "note": "'vvhere' (= where) is gapped vv + h; the vv+h cluster superficially reads like 'vyhe'; 'ioyned' = i/j"},
    {"line_index": 11, "role": "list_item", "text": "tations of Scripture, if they be vvritten thus, Gen.4,16. the firſt"},
    {"line_index": 12, "role": "list_item", "text": "is the chapter, the ſecond is the verſe. If thus, Gen.4.16. both are"},
    {"line_index": 13, "role": "list_item", "text": "the Chapters. If thus, Gen.4,16.17.18. the firſt is the chapter, al the"},
    {"line_index": 14, "role": "list_item", "text": "reſt, the verſes. If thus, Gen.4,16.5,7. it ſignifieth, chap.4. verſ.16."},
    {"line_index": 15, "role": "list_item", "text": "and chap.5. verſ.7."},
    {"line_index": 16, "role": "list_item", "text": "† This croſſe ſignifieth the beginning of euery verſe.", "marks": ["†"], "note": "† = printed dagger/cross mark in left mark-column; 'croſſe' = long-ſſ"},
    {"line_index": 17, "role": "list_item", "text": "″ This marke in the text, ſignifieth that there is an Annotation", "marks": ["″"], "note": "mark = a raised double-comma / two right-leaning strokes at cap height; '″' (U+2033) is a best-fit approximation of the printer's sort"},
    {"line_index": 18, "role": "list_item", "text": "vpon that vvord or vvordes vvhich folovv the ſaid marke.", "note": "gapped vv: vvord, vvordes, vvhich, folovv (folovv = 'follow', single l)"},
    {"line_index": 19, "role": "list_item", "text": "* This ſtarre in the text, or in the Annotatiõs, ſignifieth the allega-", "marks": ["*"], "line_end_hyphen": true, "note": "* = star/asterisk mark; 'Annotatiõs' = tilde over o (nasal abbrev, õ = on)"},
    {"line_index": 20, "role": "list_item", "text": "tions cited ouer againſt the ſame in the margent, or ſome other"},
    {"line_index": 21, "role": "list_item", "text": "thing anſvvering therevnto.", "note": "anſvvering = long-ſ + gapped vv; therevnto = u/v"},
    {"line_index": 22, "role": "list_item", "text": "⟨?⟩ This marke ſhevveth an other reading in the margent. And if", "marks": ["⟨?⟩"], "note": "left mark = a faint two-stroke mark (raised comma + hook) denoting 'an other reading'; faint inking + facing-page bleed-through prevent confident identification; ſhevveth = long-ſ + gapped vv"},
    {"line_index": 23, "role": "list_item", "text": "there be nothing in the margent, it ſignifieth that thoſe"},
    {"line_index": 24, "role": "list_item", "text": "vvordes are not in ſome copies."},
    {"line_index": 25, "role": "list_item", "text": "⁘ c b Theſe notes in the text, referre the reader to the ſelf ſame in", "marks": ["⁘", "c", "b"], "note": "marks = a four-dot square (⁘ approximates the 2x2 dot sort) followed by two superscript reference-letters 'c' and 'b'; these letters are the SUBJECT being defined (the note-keys), so kept in the legend text"},
    {"line_index": 26, "role": "list_item", "text": "the margent."},
    {"line_index": 27, "role": "list_item", "text": "Mt. for Matthevv.", "note": "Matthevv = gapped vv (Matthew)"},
    {"line_index": 28, "role": "list_item", "text": "Mr. for Marke."},
    {"line_index": 29, "role": "list_item", "text": "⊣ This marke ſignifieth the ending of Goſpels and Epiſtles.", "marks": ["⊣"], "note": "mark = a leftward-barbed end-sign (solid left arrowhead + horizontal bar + upright serifed I); '⊣' (U+22A3) is a best-fit approximation"},
    {"line_index": 30, "role": "paragraph", "text": "Their beginning is knovven by the margent, vvhere directly at", "note": "knovven, vvhere = gapped vv"},
    {"line_index": 31, "role": "paragraph", "text": "the beginning of them, is ſet, The Goſpel, or, The Epiſtle vpon ſuch a day.", "note": "italic example phrases: 'The Goſpel, or,' and 'The Epiſtle vpon ſuch a day.'"},
    {"line_index": 32, "role": "paragraph", "text": "And if it could not be ſo ſet directly (becauſe of other marginal"},
    {"line_index": 33, "role": "paragraph", "text": "notes) then b is the marke of their beginning. And if ſome fevv", "note": "'b' = superscript reference-letter (the beginning-mark being defined); fevv = gapped vv"},
    {"line_index": 34, "role": "paragraph", "text": "by ouerſight be not noted in the margent, it is ſupplied in the table"},
    {"line_index": 35, "role": "paragraph", "text": "of Epiſtles and Goſpels, at the end of this booke."},
    {"line_index": 36, "role": "signature", "text": "d", "note": "gathering signature at foot-centre"},
    {"line_index": 37, "role": "catchword", "text": "THE", "excluded_reason": "reader/binder catchword at foot-right; next page (idx 25) opens 'THE BOOKES OF THE NEVV Teſtament'; excluded from body concatenation"}
  ],
  "intervals": [
    {"idx": 0, "kind": "heading", "text": "THE SIGNIFICATION OR MEANING OF THE NVMBERS AND MARKES vſed in this Nevv Teſtament.", "lines": [0, 1, 2]},
    {"idx": 1, "kind": "list_item", "text": "THE numbers in the inner margent of the text, ſhevv the number of verſes in euery Chapter.", "lines": [3, 4]},
    {"idx": 2, "kind": "list_item", "text": "The numbers in the Arguments before euery Chapter, point to the ſame numbers of verſes in the text, treating of the ſame matter.", "lines": [5, 6, 7]},
    {"idx": 3, "kind": "list_item", "text": "The numbers in the beginning of the Annotations, ſignifie, that the Annotation is vpon ſuch a verſe of the text.", "lines": [8, 9]},
    {"idx": 4, "kind": "list_item", "text": "The numbers in the inner margent, or els vvhere, ioyned to the citations of Scripture, if they be vvritten thus, Gen.4,16. the firſt is the chapter, the ſecond is the verſe. If thus, Gen.4.16. both are the Chapters. If thus, Gen.4,16.17.18. the firſt is the chapter, al the reſt, the verſes. If thus, Gen.4,16.5,7. it ſignifieth, chap.4. verſ.16. and chap.5. verſ.7.", "lines": [10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15]},
    {"idx": 5, "kind": "list_item", "text": "† This croſſe ſignifieth the beginning of euery verſe.", "lines": [16]},
    {"idx": 6, "kind": "list_item", "text": "″ This marke in the text, ſignifieth that there is an Annotation vpon that vvord or vvordes vvhich folovv the ſaid marke.", "lines": [17, 18]},
    {"idx": 7, "kind": "list_item", "text": "* This ſtarre in the text, or in the Annotatiõs, ſignifieth the allegations cited ouer againſt the ſame in the margent, or ſome other thing anſvvering therevnto.", "lines": [19, 20, 21]},
    {"idx": 8, "kind": "list_item", "text": "⟨?⟩ This marke ſhevveth an other reading in the margent. And if there be nothing in the margent, it ſignifieth that thoſe vvordes are not in ſome copies.", "lines": [22, 23, 24]},
    {"idx": 9, "kind": "list_item", "text": "⁘ c b Theſe notes in the text, referre the reader to the ſelf ſame in the margent.", "lines": [25, 26]},
    {"idx": 10, "kind": "list_item", "text": "Mt. for Matthevv.", "lines": [27]},
    {"idx": 11, "kind": "list_item", "text": "Mr. for Marke.", "lines": [28]},
    {"idx": 12, "kind": "list_item", "text": "⊣ This marke ſignifieth the ending of Goſpels and Epiſtles.", "lines": [29]},
    {"idx": 13, "kind": "paragraph", "text": "Their beginning is knovven by the margent, vvhere directly at the beginning of them, is ſet, The Goſpel, or, The Epiſtle vpon ſuch a day. And if it could not be ſo ſet directly (becauſe of other marginal notes) then b is the marke of their beginning. And if ſome fevv by ouerſight be not noted in the margent, it is ſupplied in the table of Epiſtles and Goſpels, at the end of this booke.", "lines": [30, 31, 32, 33, 34, 35]}
  ],
  "uncertain": [
    {"line_index": 0, "span": "V THE SIGNIFICATION", "note": "a dark, forward-reading 'V' sits at the far left before 'THE'. It is offset/set-off (ink transfer) from the facing recto ('THE BOOKES OF THE NEVV Teſtament'), NOT part of this centred heading. Excluded from the heading text."},
    {"line_index": 10, "span": "vvhere", "note": "= 'where' (or els where = or elsewhere). Set as gapped vv + h; the second v's right stroke + the h's short ascender make the cluster superficially read 'vyhe'. Transcribed 'vvhere' per the visible two v-sorts."},
    {"line_index": 16, "span": "croſſe", "note": "double s in 'crosse' read as long-ſ + long-ſ (ſſ). Second ſ is pre-e; flagged though ascenders on both are visible."},
    {"line_index": 17, "span": "″ (annotation mark)", "note": "the mark for 'annotation upon that word' is a raised double-comma / two short right-leaning strokes at cap height. No clean Unicode; '″' (U+2033 double prime) used as best-fit. Glyph SHAPE is legible; exact codepoint is an approximation."},
    {"line_index": 22, "span": "⟨?⟩ (other-reading mark)", "note": "the mark for 'an other reading in the margent' could not be confidently identified. Enhanced/zoomed it shows two faint strokes (a raised comma + a small hook/curl, possibly over dots), but the light inking and heavy facing-page bleed-through leave the exact form ambiguous — possibly a double-comma akin to line 17's mark, or a distinct comma+hook/dotted sign. Flagged rather than guessed."},
    {"line_index": 25, "span": "⁘ c b (these-notes marks)", "note": "leftmost mark is four dots in a 2x2 square; '⁘' (U+2058) approximates it. Followed by two small superscript reference-letters 'c' and 'b' (examples of the marginal note-keys). Kept in text because they are the marks being DEFINED by this legend entry, not apparatus keying scripture."},
    {"line_index": 29, "span": "⊣ (end-of-Gospel/Epistle mark)", "note": "the 'ending of Goſpels and Epiſtles' mark is a leftward-barbed sign: a solid left-pointing arrowhead + a short horizontal bar + an upright serifed I. No clean Unicode; '⊣' (U+22A3 left tack) used as best-fit. Shape legible; codepoint approximate."},
    {"line_index": 11, "span": "Gen.4,16. / Gen.4.16. / Gen.4,16.17.18. / Gen.4,16.5,7.", "note": "citation exemplars (entry 4). The semantic distinction is the separator: comma between chapter,verse (4,16) vs period between two chapters (4.16). Micro-spacing around the periods/commas in the numeric citations is tight on the page and rendered tight here; exact intra-citation spacing is low-confidence."}
  ],
  "observer": "agent:matter-nt-signification-or-meaning",
  "observed_at": "2026-07-20",
  "method": "Visual-multimodal diplomatic read of the native-res jp2 (jp2-S08 page 24) in 5 full-width horizontal bands + targeted high-zoom and contrast-enhanced micro-crops for the mark-column glyphs and w/vv calls (per the brief's efficiency rule; no dictionary normalization). FOUR VALIDATIONS: (1) LOCALIZATION PASS — heading reads exactly 'THE SIGNIFICATION OR MEANING OF THE NVMBERS AND MARKES vſed in this Nevv Teſtament.' and the body is the legend of numbers/marks (†, *, note-letters, Mt./Mr., end-mark); this is the section requested, not a lookalike. (2) IDENTITY PASS — 1582 Rhemes New Testament, scan S8, ocr_dir jp2-S08, source 1582_Rhemes_New_Testament_0024.jp2; the small vv-fount and display 'Nevv Teſtament' match the 1582 Rhemes founts. (3) PLACEMENT PASS — no printed folio; gathering signature 'd' at foot-centre and catchword 'THE' at foot-right; page_index 24 sits between the Preface (idx 23) and 'THE BOOKES OF THE NEVV Teſtament' (idx 25, which the catchword 'THE' anticipates). (4) COMPLETENESS PASS — the entire Signification section is contained on this ONE page; it does not continue (next page begins a different section). long-ſ read glyph-driven; w/vv read per-glyph (all gapped vv here). Reference not needed (self-evident legend text).",
  "confidence": "high on the display heading and all prose/legend body text (clear medium/small roman, well-inked); high on the w/vv determination (uniformly gapped vv across the page). LOWER confidence on three special mark-glyphs: line 17 (″, double-comma mark) and line 29 (⊣, end-mark) have legible SHAPES but approximated Unicode; line 22 mark is genuinely unresolved (faint + bleed-through) and flagged ⟨?⟩. Intra-citation micro-spacing (line 11/interval 4) is low-confidence.",
  "glyph_regime_resolved": "NT-1582 Signification page = SINGLE gapped-vv regime. This page is set in the SMALL legend roman fount, which patterns with the Preface's small dense-measure + marginal-note fount (declared 'w'->'vv'), NOT the Preface's large connected-w drop-cap fount. EVERY lowercase double-v on the page is visibly GAPPED (daylight between the two v-sorts): ſhevv, vvhere, vvritten, vvord, vvordes, vvhich, folovv, anſvvering, ſhevveth, vvordes, Matthevv, knovven, fevv; and the display 'Nevv Teſtament' is gapped VV (titling fount has no W sort). No connected-w sort observed anywhere on this page, so 'vv' is transcribed page-wide per the per-glyph pixel rule (§w-regime). NOTE: the 2026-07-18 ratification 'matter-nt prose = connected w' is fount-specific to the Preface BODY paragraph and does NOT extend to this smaller legend fount — the pixels here decide vv. long-ſ read glyph-driven (§long-ſ): kept where the sort has an ascender (ſhevv, verſes, ſignifieth, croſſe, thoſe, ſelf, Goſpel, Epiſtle, becauſe, etc.). u/v and i/j preserved as printed (vpon, vſed, euery, ouer, therevnto, ioyned). Tilde nasal-abbrev preserved (Annotatiõs)."
}
